      "title": "Student Teaching Supervisor",
      "description": "Student Teaching Supervisor - ADJUNCT POSITION - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Student Teaching Supervisor – ADJUNCT POSITION Position Title : Student Teaching Supervisor Department : Education Division Position Requirements and Preferences Education : Master’s Degree in education with training and recent experience (within 5 years) in the content area and grade level of supervision. Experience: Three years of teaching experience in the content area and grade level of supervision. Abilities: Proficiency in Google Docs Ability to travel to school districts Good communication and interpersonal skills Independent decision making, ability to exercise good judgment, accuracy flexibility, and well-developed critical thinking skills Knowledge of online instructional learning modalities and best practices Excellent professional interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills Commitment to maintaining consistently high professional standards Demonstrate the ability to work collaboratively with a growing, innovative team A commitment to working with a diverse population of students is essential demonstrated experience in this area is preferred Works harmoniously with others Performs in a manner that benefits student learning Position Summary: Student Teaching Supervisors oversee student teachers across the state a minimum of once every 10 school days per placement and provide feedback to the student teachers in accordance with Iowa Code Chapter 79. Responsibilities: Participate in Supervisor Training Conduct face-to-face supervision of student teachers once every 10 school days per placement Conduct a face-to-face or zoom call for the first initial meeting Write up feedback after each observation and submit it to the student teacher, cooperating teacher, and student teaching placement coordinator Review weekly lesson plans, provide feedback, and grade Read and respond to weekly journals, provide feedback and grade Complete the final paperwork and submit to Student Teaching Coordinator. Satisfy 40-hour teaching or co-teaching requirement within five years. Reports to : Education Student Teaching Coordinator Start Date: TBD Replacement or New Position : Replacement Closing Date of Posting : Until Filled This position is paid as an independent contractor. William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Proposed Schedule This is a contracted 8-week or 16-week placement assignment with flexible hours during the day. – Exempt employee Any interested applicants should send their CV to Myron McReynolds at myron.mcreynolds@wmpenn.edu Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/adjunct-instructor-in-english-adjunct-faculty-position/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor in English",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor in English - ADJUNCT FACULTY POSITION - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Adjunct Instructor in English – ADJUNCT FACULTY POSITION JOB TITLE: Adjunct Instructor in English JOB SUMMARY: Teach introductory and college level writing courses. DEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs – Humanities QUALIFICATIONS: Masters in English or a related degree and teaching experience. A. Education M.A. B. Teaching Experience C. Abilities – Guide and inspire students REPORTS TO: Humanities Division Chair PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES: A. Provide an education with a Leadership and Technology focus, and enliven that provision through adherence to the Quaker principles of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. B. Represents the College in a positive manner with prospective, current, and former students, employees, and the community. C. Demonstrates enthusiasm, self-motivation, and a positive attitude in meeting and dealing effectively and courteously with students, other personnel, and all members of the community. D. Interprets departmental and/or college policies and procedures. E. Works harmoniously with others. F. Performs in a manner which benefits student learning. G. This position may require travel. H. This position may require occasional weekend and evening hours. I. Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION: Performance of this position will be evaluated in accordance with the policies established by the Board of Directors of William Penn University. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Please send a letter of interest and your academic or professional credentials to: Dr. Wilton Wright,  Humanities Division Chair Wilton.Wright@wmpenn.edu Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/employment/clinical-instructor-nursing-fp/": {
      "title": "Clinical Instructor - Nursing",
      "description": "Clinical Instructor - Nursing - Faculty Position - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Clinical Instructor – Nursing – Faculty Position Position Title: Nursing Clinical Instructor Department: Nursing Position Description: Reports to the Division Chair of Nursing with indirect supervision provided by the Clinical Simulation Lab Coordinator for the implementation of the approved curriculum based on the mission and philosophy of the nursing program and the College. This is a hourly contractual position August-July Provides students with opportunities to acquire the knowledge and practice the skills identified in course objectives using varied and appropriate teaching methods. Plan learning activities to meet program outcomes based on the standards set by policies, legal and other regularity requirements, and acceptable practices. Participates in the program evaluation and continuous improvement process and engage in personal professional development. Requirements: Completion of an accredited professional nursing education program. BSN with concentration/experience in clinical area of teaching (med-surg, OB, peds, etc) Experience of at least two years in the practice of nursing as a registered nurse within the last five years. Hold a current Iowa active unencumbered license as a registered nurse. Previous teaching experience preferred or currently attending a course offered by an accredited school in teaching. Excellent written and oral communication and analytical skills. Functional abilities to carry out classroom, clinical and laboratory teaching responsibilities. Competence in clinical skills in areas of teaching. Competent in personal computer applications; word processing, spreadsheet, database, and email. Successful completion of criminal background check and drug screening required current American Heart Association CPR. Provide evidence of yearly tuberculin skin tests, and other required immunizations as per nursing program policy Essential Duties & Responsibilities: Provides clinical instruction to students in approved health care settings, adhering to the policies of the clinical setting and the College. Participate in College and/or DON committee assignments Clinical experiences may be facility assigned or completed in the clinical simulation lab as assigned. Clinical instructors will be available to work in the Clinical Simulation Lab as assigned for clinical expectations. Discuss with students their concerns and/or problems directly or indirectly related to learning experience. Is responsible to assist the student to develop an understanding of values, attitudes, and ideals appropriate to the health care profession. Establish and maintain relationships with new and existing clinical sites. To participate in faculty meetings, both formally and informally with didactic and clinical faculty members. Provide clinical, classroom, and clinical simulation lab instruction. Supervise student groups in clinical areas (maintains presence in the facility during entire student clinical time if not precepted). Orient students to the clinical area and demonstrate proper procedures. Responsible for producing and distributing course learning objectives and student schedules to the clinical facilities prior to student attendance at the facility. Lead discussions and elicit information from students which demonstrate that students are learning and accomplishing the clinical objectives. Maintain clinical standards and course expectations throughout each course or term. Evaluate and grade student performance. Meets with students at midterm for formal evaluation and again at the end of the course as to progress and performance. Maintain the professional practice knowledge base needed to instruct learners in contemporary nursing practice. Communicate with Clinical Simulation Lab Coordinator or Division Chair as necessary to resolve issues or concerns in clinical areas. Work effectively as part of the overall faculty team demonstrating positive interpersonal relations, collaborating with other faculty members to meet student needs, participating in faculty meetings and nursing program committees and responding to requests from management. Participate in ongoing program evaluation activities as needed. Maintain faculty expectations as required by the College and the Board of Nursing. Demonstrate proper respect for students, faculty, and staff and has student-friendly manner in the conduct of class. Other as assigned Reports to: Nursing Division Chair Start Date: Immediately Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time / Part-Time / Temp: Part-time Closing Date of Posting: Until filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/admissions-counselor-staff-position/": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Admissions Counselor - Staff Position - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Admissions Counselor – Staff Position JOB TITLE : Admissions Counselor JOB SUMMARY : WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, the Admissions Counselor will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Specifically, the Admissions Counselor will effectively communicate the opportunities that the institution offers to students through face-to-face contact, phone calls and electronic exchanges to help guide students and their families through the admissions process. This employee will also support university processes to achieve educational and economic goals. DEPARTMENT : Admissions QUALIFICATIONS : Education Bachelor’s degree required. Experience Admissions experience not required; personal experience as a WPU student is preferred. Abilities Enthusiasm for working with students and their families Ability to facilitate, manage and evaluate assigned recruitment area Ability to work in an environment of shifting priorities, frequent interruptions, hectic pace, high level of interaction with students, staff and/or the public. Working knowledge of computer software programs which may include Word, Excel, institutional mainframe computer system software, or similar programs. Ability to learn and retain a wide range of institutional information Excellent written communication skills including proficiency in business English, grammar, punctuation, and spelling. Excellent oral communication skills including phone and in-person conversations and ability to give presentations in small and large group settings Ability to handle highly confidential matters and materials with discretion. Ability to work independently as well as be a collaborative team player in completing assigned tasks and meeting deadlines. Ability to work with diverse populations, including a sensitivity to their needs and concerns Excellent customer service skills including phone and in-person reception etiquette. Proficiency with office machines including fax, scanner and copy machine. A valid driver’s license. REPORTS TO : Director of Admissions and/or Vice President for Enrollment Management PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES: Assume a key role in the admissions activities of the University through management of an assigned recruiting territory, including correspondence, telephone and personal contact with students. Assist prospective students and their parents through the enrollment process, explaining academic programs, admissions requirements, and basic financial aid information. Visit high schools and serve as a liaison with guidance counselors; represent the University at college fairs statewide. Represents the University in a positive manner with prospective, current, and former students, employees, and the community. Demonstrates enthusiasm, self-motivation, and a positive attitude in meeting and dealing effectively and courteously with students, other personnel, and all members of the community. Interprets departmental and/or college policies and procedures. Works harmoniously with others. Some evening and weekend commitments are required; as is occasional overnight travel Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION: Performance of this position will be evaluated in accordance with the policies established by the Board of Directors of William Penn University. Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
