nd actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Responsibilities: Patrols campus to assure all University buildings and facilities are secure Enforce University rules, policies, and procedures Monitors security cameras Prepare and maintains shift logs, calls for service, and incident reports. Conduct monthly building fire safety inspections. Identify hazards that pose a threat to students & employees. Reports to: Campus Safety Director Start Date: April 11, 2022 Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time/Part-time/Temp: Part-Time Closing Date of Posting: Until Filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
