Position Summary: WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all of its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and help others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Responsibilities: Work a minimum of 30 hours per week. Work with admissions counselors, professors, coaches/sponsors to make prospective students’ campus visits positive. Creating a safe, clean and enjoyable environment for all students and visitors. Assist with coordination of campus visit days for prospective freshmen and transfer students Assist with coordination of campus visit days for prospective students in certain academic programs or extracurricular activities (i.e. Nursing Day or Football Recruitment Day) reate and update student records in database Monitor inventory of promotional materials; make recommendations for reordering Represents the University in a positive manner with prospective, current, and former students, employees, and the community. Demonstrates enthusiasm, self-motivation, and a positive attitude in meeting and dealing effectively and courteously with students, other personnel, and all members of the community. Works harmoniously with others. Arrange on-campus accommodations for prospective students Be a positive role model for students. Assist with inventory and assessment of equipment. Conduct self in a professional manner at all times. All Other duties as assigned. Reports to: Director of Admissions Supervises: Assigned Work-Study Employees Evaluation: Performance will be the responsibility of the Director of Admissions. Send cover letter, resume and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, Iowa 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/advancement-ga/": {
      "title": "Advancement - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Advancement - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Advancement – Graduate Assistant JOB TITLE : Graduate Assistant – Advancement Office JOB SUMMARY : The Advancement Office Graduate Assistant supports the University’s efforts to build meaningful relationships with alumni, donors, and friends of William Penn University. This position provides administrative, communications, event, and project support while contributing to fundraising, alumni engagement, donor stewardship, and other initiatives that advance the University’s mission. DEPARTMENT : Advancement QUALIFICATIONS : Education – Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Acceptance into a William Penn University graduate program. Must maintain the minimum cumulative GPA required by William Penn University to remain eligible for graduate assistantship employment. Abilities – Must maintain confidentiality of sensitive information and data. Assist with data entry, database maintenance, and record updates in CAMS. Support alumni and donor research, including address verification and profile updates. Assist with donor stewardship efforts, including mailings, filing, and other office support tasks. Help create, edit, or organize marketing and promotional materials, including graphics, apparel designs, and other print or digital content. Assist with event planning, preparation, and execution for Advancement and alumni activities. Compile information, stories, surveys, reports, and other materials as needed. Provide general administrative support to the Advancement Office. Serve as a welcoming ambassador for William Penn University by interacting professionally with alumni, donors, students, and campus visitors, including giving campus tours when requested. Promote William Penn University, its programs, and the student experience. Conduct yourself in a professional manner at all times. Perform other duties as assigned. Experience – Previous customer service, hospitality, or office experience is encouraged but not required. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to prioritize multiple tasks. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and a willingness to learn new software and technologies. REPORTS TO : Executive Vice President for Advancement PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES : Provide an education with a Leadership and Technology focus, and enliven that provision through adherence to the Quaker principles of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Represent the University in a positive manner with prospective, current, and former students, employees, alumni, donors, and the community. Demonstrate enthusiasm, self-motivation, and a positive attitude in meeting and dealing effectively and courteously with students, other personnel, and all members of the community. Interpret departmental and/or University policies and procedures. Work harmoniously with others. Perform in a manner which benefits student learning. This position may require travel. This position may require occasional weekend and evening hours. Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION : Performance of this position will be evaluated in accordance with the policies established by the Board of Directors of William Penn University. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT : At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/womens-wrestling-graduate-assistant": {
      "title": "Women’s Wrestling – Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Women’s Wrestling – Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Women’s Wrestling – Graduate Assistant JOB TITLE : Women’s Wrestling GA JOB SUMMARY : WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all of its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. DEPARMENT : Women’s Wrestling – Athletics QUALIFICATIONS : A. Education Bachelor’s Degree required B. Experience Background in the sport of Wrestling C. Abilities • Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams; • Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment; • Good written and oral communication skills; • Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; • Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills essential; • Willing to work long hours. REPORTS TO : Jake Kadel SUPERVISES : Assigned Athletes PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES : A. Administer your sport in total compliance with William Penn, NAIA and HAAC regulations and guidelines. B. Monitor and stay within the parameters of the Women’s Wrestling budget. All purchases need to be approved by the head coach. C. Assist with recruiting and retaining student-athletes. D. Attend Athletic Department meetings. E. Assist with coordination of travel plans with the Transportation Director. F. Be a positive role model for athletes and monitor discipline procedures within your sport. G. Encourage/monitor attendance and academic performance as directed by the head coach. H. Assist with annual inventory. I. Conduct yourself in a professional manner and display good sportsmanship at all times. J. Fulfill all obligations, as established by your program, for the NAIA Champions of Character initiative. K. Be loyal and supportive of the Staff, Faculty and Administration. L. Always follow the Chain of Command. M. Cooperate and communicate with the Training Staff N. Assist with the supervision of other athletic events as needed by the administration. O. All Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION : Performance will be the responsibility of the Head Coach. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT : At will employee. William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Date: {3/17/25} Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/employment/track-field-ga/": {
      "title": "Track & Field - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Track & Field - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Track & Field – Graduate Assistant Date: June 8, 2023 Positions Title: Track & Field Graduate Assistants (2 openings) Department: Athletics Positions Requirements & Preferences: Education Bachelor’s Degree required Experience Background in the area of your assigned Graduate Assistant area (Track & Field) Abilities Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams; Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment; Good written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills essential; Willing to work long hours. Position Summary: William Penn University strives to create a vibrant learning community for all of its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, our Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Responsibilities: Administer your sport/area in total compliance with William Penn, NAIA and HAAC regulations and guidelines. Monitor and stay within the parameters of the designated budget. All purchases need to be approved by the head coach/department head. Assist with recruiting and retaining students. Oversee Junior Varsity program, when applicable. Attend Department meetings. Assist with coordination of travel plans with the Transportation Director. Be a positive role model for students and monitor discipline procedures within your sport/area. Encourage/monitor attendance and academic performance as directed by the head coach/department head. Assist with annual inventory. Conduct yourself in a professional manner and display good sportsmanship at all times. Fulfill all obligations, as established by your program, for the NAIA Champions of Character initiative. Be loyal and supportive of the Staff, Faculty and Administration. Cooperate and communicate with the Training Staff. Perform responsibilities of a Campus Security Authority (CSA) and attend annual training. Assist with the supervision of other athletic/university events as needed by the administration. All Other duties as assigned Reports to: Head Track & Field Coach Start Date: Immediately Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time | Part-Time | Temp: Graduate Assistant (minimum of 2 years) Closing Date of Posting: Until Filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/employment/mens-bowling-ga/": {
      "title": "Men’s Bowling - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Men’s Bowling - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Men’s Bowling – Graduate Assistant Date: April 12, 2023 Position Title: Men’s Bowling Graduate Assistant Department: Athletics Position Requirements and Preferences: Education: Bachelor’s Degree required Experience: Background in the sport of Bowling Abilities: Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams; Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment; Good written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills essential; Willing to work long hours. Position Summary: WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all of its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Responsibilities: Administer your sport in total compliance with William Penn, NAIA and HAAC regulations and guidelines. Monitor and stay within the parameters of the Bowling budget. All purchases need to be approved by the head coach. Assist with recruiting and retaining student-athletes. Attend Athletic Department meetings. Assist with coordination of travel plans with the Transportation Director. Be a positive role model for athletes and monitor discipline procedures within your sport. Encourage/monitor attendance and academic performance as directed by the head coach. Assist with annual inventory. Conduct yourself in a professional manner and display good sportsmanship at all times. Fulfill all obligations, as established by your program, for the NAIA Champions of Character initiative. Be loyal and supportive of the Staff, Faculty and Administration. Always follow the Chain of Command. Cooperate and communicate with the Training Staff Assist with the supervision of other athletic events as needed by the administration. All Other duties as assigned. Reports to: Head Coach for Men’s Bowling Start Date: August 1, 2023 Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time | Part-Time | Temp: Graduate Assistants (2 year minimum) Closing Date of Position: Until Filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/mens-soccer-graduate-assistant/": {
      "title": "Men’s Soccer - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Men’s Soccer - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Men’s Soccer – Graduate Assistant JOB TITLE: Men’s Soccer Graduate Assistant JOB SUMMARY: WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all of its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. DEPARMENT: Men’s Soccer – Athletics QUALIFICATIONS: A. Education Bachelor’s Degree required B. Experience Background in the sport of Soccer C. Abilities • Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams; • Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment; • Good written and oral communication skills; • Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; • Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills essential; • Willing to work long hours. REPORTS TO: Head Coach, Assistant Coach SUPERVISES: Assigned Athletes PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES: A. Administer your sport in total compliance with William Penn, NAIA and HAAC regulations and guidelines. B. Monitor and stay within the parameters of the soccer budget. All purchases need to be approved by the head coach. C. Responsible for running individual and position orientated film-review sessions. D. Assist with recruiting and retaining student-athletes. E. Attend Athletic Department meetings. F. Assist with coordination of travel plans with the Transportation Director. G. Be a positive role model for athletes and monitor discipline procedures within your sport. H. Encourage/monitor attendance and academic performance as directed by the head coach. I. Assist with annual inventory. J. Conduct yourself in a professional manner and display good sportsmanship at all times. K. Fulfill all obligations, as established by your program, for the NAIA Champions of Character initiative. L. Be loyal and supportive of the Staff, Faculty and Administration. M. Always follow the Chain of Command. N. Cooperate and communicate with the Training Staff O. Assist with the supervision of other athletic events as needed by the administration. P. All Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION: Performance will be the responsibility of the Head Coach. TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT: At will employee. William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/online-graduate-assistant/": {
      "title": "Online – Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Online – Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Online – Graduate Assistant JOB TITLE: Graduate Assistant Online Program JOB SUMMARY: William Penn University strives to create a vibrant learning community for all its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. DEPARMENT: Online Program QUALIFICATIONS: A. Education Bachelor’s Degree required B. Experience Background in your assigned Graduate Assistant area C. Abilities • Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams. • Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment. • Good written and oral communication skills. • Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meet deadlines. • Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills are essential. • Willing to work flexible hours. REPORTS TO: Online Director SUPERVISES: Assigned students PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES: Student Support A. Communication: Act as the first point of contact for student inquiries via email, phone, or online platforms. Respond promptly to student questions, concerns, and requests for assistance. B. Orientation: Assist in the creation and delivery of online orientation materials for new students. Guide students through the online learning platform and familiarize them with course expectations and resources. C. Advising: Provide academic advising and support to online students, helping them navigate courses and the use of services. Online Program Coordination D. Resource Development: Contribute to the development and updating of online program resources, such as handbooks, guides, and instructional videos. E. Data Management: Maintain accurate records of student enrollment, attendance, and performance. Assist with data collection and reporting for program evaluation. Engagement and Community Building F. Events: Organize and participate in virtual events, workshops, and webinars to engage online students and foster a sense of community. G. Communication Channels: Manage online communication channels, such as discussion forums and social media groups, to promote interaction and collaboration among students. H. Networking Opportunities: Assist students in connecting with peers, alumni, and industry professionals to enhance their learning experience and career opportunities. I. All Other duties as assigned. EVALUATION: Performance will be the responsibility of the Online Director TERMS OF EMPLOYMENT: At will employee. Send cover letter, resume and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, Iowa 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/employment/campus-ministry-ga/": {
      "title": "Campus Ministry - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Campus Ministry - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Campus Ministry – Graduate Assistant Date : June 21, 2023 Position Title: Campus Ministry Graduate Assistant Department: Student Services Position Requirements and Preferences: Education: Bachelor’s Degree required Experience: Background with Spiritual Leadership Abilities: Demonstrated talent in building cohesive teams; Independent decision making and ability to exercise good judgment; Good written and oral communication skills; Ability to work independently and as a team member to complete assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; Organizational skills, time management, relationship building, and communication skills essential; Willing to work long hours. Position Summary: WPU strives to create a vibrant learning community for all its members, including students, staff, and faculty. To help foster that community, Graduate Assistants will lead by example and develop others’ leadership capabilities, employ relevant technologies, and actively demonstrate the Quaker virtues of simplicity, peace-making, integrity, community, and equality. Responsibilities: Administer your spiritual life responsibilities in total compliance with William Penn and Campus Ministry Committee regulations and guidelines. Work with Youth and Young Adults Director of Iowa Yearly Meeting of Friends as well as the pastor of College Avenue Friends. Monitor and stay within the parameters of the campus ministries budget. All purchases need to be approved by the Director of Student Activities. Assist with recruiting and retaining religious life scholarship students while developing leaders and spiritual growth. Attend Campus Ministry Committee meetings. Cooperate and communicate with the Campus Ministry Committee. Assist with coordination of travel plans with the Transportation Director. Be a positive role model for students and monitor discipline procedures as outlined by Religious Life scholarships and William Penn University Code of Conduct. Encourage/monitor attendance and academic performance of Spiritual Life students. Conduct yourself in a professional manner with integrity at all times. Fulfill all obligations, as established by your program. Be loyal and supportive of the Staff, Faculty and Administration. Always follow the Chain of Command. Follow all University policies and procedures. Perform responsibility of a Campus Security Authority (CSA) and attend annual training. Initiate and execute activities that further the spiritual lives of students. All Other duties as assigned. Reports to: Campus Minister Start Date: Immediately Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time/Part-Time/Temp: Minimum of Two Years (Temporary) Closing Date of Posting: Until Filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee. William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/employment/career-services-ga/": {
      "title": "Career Services - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Career Services - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Career Services – Graduate Assistant Date: May 04, 2023 Position Title: Career Services Graduate Assistant Department: Student Services Position Requirements and Preferences: Education: Bachelor’s Degree Experience: Background in Business, or Marketing preferred but not required. Abilities: Must be enrolled full-time in a Graduate degree program. Possess excellent oral and written skills. Position Summary: The graduate assistant aids the Career Services department in the overall development and management of a comprehensive, centralized career development and career services program. Responsibilities: Work 20 hours per week. Completes training component related to Career Services and available tools. Provides individual and group career counseling to students and alumni to assist with career decision-making. Administers career assessments (such as COPS) as requested, and helps students interpret them. Assists in research, design and delivery of workshops, class presentations and panels on career-related issues, including self-assessment, career exploration, job search strategies including use of the Internet, graduate school, and overall professional preparation. Oversees and promotes online career mentoring process for use by current students and alumni in collaboration with Alumni Relations and the Office of Advancement. Assists with the coordination of career planning days. Cultivates and monitors partnerships with faculty, current and potential internship sites, employers and alumni. Attends Connect Iowa meetings, as appropriate, and seminars, conferences, and webinars related to Career Services. Encourages students to engage in information interviews, job shadowing, etc. with alumni and employers. Assists in the development and implementation of marketing strategies of career services to students, faculty, employers and alumni, including use of social networking sites. Advises and coaches students on resume and letter writing, networking and interviewing, and the use of online tools like Handshake and social media tools such as Facebook, Twitter, and LinkedIn. Consistently demonstrates a positive attitude. Must be open and adaptable to change. Must work cooperatively and respectfully with all populations. May supervise Career Services work/study student in absence of Coordinator. Performs other related duties as assigned by Career Services Coordinator. Reports to: Director of Career Services Start Date: September 1, 2023 Replacement or New Position: Replacement Full-Time | Part-Time | Temp: Graduate Assistant (Temporary) Closing Date of Position: Until Filled Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    },
    "https://www.wmpenn.edu/student-success-program-graduate-assistant": {
      "title": "Student Success Program - Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Student Success Program - Graduate Assistant - William Penn University Skip to Content Apply Admissions & Aid Apply Financial Aid Transfer to William Penn Federal Work-Study Program Military Benefits Scholarships Tuition Viewbook Welcome to Admissions Academics Academic Information Applied Technology Business Administration Education Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Studies Humanities Kinesiology and Life Sciences New Media Nursing Online Penn Leadership Core Social & Behavioral Sciences Online Education Online Degree (Distance Learning) Graduate Degrees Undergraduate Degrees Athletics Booster Club News Schedule Statesmen Live Student Life Athletic Bands Campus Ministry Campus Safety Counseling Center Housing Student Forms Student Services Student Spotlights Student Organizations Support Services Student Activities Weather and Emergency Notifications Get to Know WPU Presidential Search A William Penn University Story Accreditation & Institutional Research Mission & History Visit Campus Consumer Information Contact & Directory Explore Oskaloosa Employment Events Calendar News Make a Gift Alumni Alumni Events Alumni Registry Alumni Success Stories Bulletin Donate to William Penn Get Involved Hall of Fame Penn Apparel Transcript Requests Support Penn Penn Links Search Make a Gift Penn Links WPU Access Support Services Wilcox Library Bookstore Toggle navigation Student Success Program – Graduate Assistant JOB TITLE: Student Success Program Graduate Assistant JOB SUMMARY: The Student Success Program Graduate Assistant (GA) of William Penn University is responsible for helping students achieve their academic goals. The GA provides personal and individualized guidance by scheduling and conducting one-on-one meetings with students on academic probation and at-risk students entered into the program by Administration, advisors or coaches. The GA is the point of contact for the Academic Skill Center Tutors and will maintain the functionality of the ASC. REPORTS TO : Director/Asst Director of the Student Success Program DEPARTMENT : Retention QUALIFICATIONS : A. Education Currently pursuing MBL or MSM required B. Experience Experience working with students, faculty, staff, and employers; as well as experience working with activities and special events preferred. C. Abilities Office management/coordination abilities; Genuine interest in serving students; Ability to handle highly confidential matters and materials with discretion; Ability to work independently and collaboratively in completing assigned tasks and meeting deadlines; Independent decision making, ability to exercise good judgment, accuracy, flexibility and well developed critical thinking skills; Ability to work in an environment of shifting priorities, frequent interruptions, hectic pace, high level of interaction with students, staff and/or the public Working knowledge of computer software programs which may include Microsoft Office programs, learning-management programs, or other institutional software; Excellent written  and oral communication skills; Strong data collection, analysis, and report writing skills; Excellent customer service skills including phone and in-person reception etiquette. Proficiency with office copy machine. Is an effective team player. RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform the duties of an Academic Coach with a focus on International Students Point of Contact for ASC tutors Conduct one-on-one meetings with students on Academic Probation and Academic Warning Determine through discussion any problems or issues program students may have that could hinder or prevent their academic success Give encouragement and/or direction to help students toward personal and academic success Monitor students’ grades in their academic classes Monitor students’ weekly class attendance Make appropriate referrals (counseling, Financial Aid, advisors, coaches, etc.) to students as needed Coordinate with instructors and coaches to determine and supply students’ academic needs Maintain files, reports, statistics, and documents relating to the program Collect and compile data to create semester/annual reports on the use, performance, and direction of program as indicated by the Director of the Student Success Program Coordinate with appropriate agencies to ensure proper equipment and software maintenance Act as point of contact for students identified as at-risk and/or students who are identified as needing academic follow up by faculty Assists Director in the oversight of the Academic Skill Center Performs duties of an academic tutor as needed Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of the Student Success Program and Dean of Students Send cover letter, resume, and references to: Human Resources William Penn University 201 Trueblood Ave Oskaloosa, IA 52577 johnsonb@wmpenn.edu Terms of Employment: At will employee William Penn University is an equal opportunity provider and employer. Apply Request Info Visit William Penn University 201 Trueblood Avenue Oskaloosa, IA 52577 800.779.7366 webadmin@wmpenn.edu Novel Coronavirus (COVID-19) Weather & Emergency Notifications Consumer Information"
    }
